{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact M7 head 03811c1eec370f305473733f2b58ea84a9229624 on builder/typed-core-m7-20261107, tree 1a5d8ede, all 41 paths, for request 11fbfe04 under promise 8232842a and review request 60bf4e1d. That includes the three source seals for judge.ts, genesis.ts and core.ts:Scope. Native hooks and capability arguments now run from records captured at admission. For every definition the validator admits, judgments, callback calls and validation output equal main's. Two lookups now return nothing where main threw or ran a check. Neither is reachable today. M8 must make both fail closed (findings F1 and F2 below).\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main 360014b4 is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 41 artifact paths: derive source and tests, one line each in replay/src/verify.ts and scope/src/core.ts, the seal test, the generated Page module, the note and nine manifests. The commit-message check passes: 16 checked, 0 flagged. No dependency, lockfile, gate script, grant, wire type or Wrangler file changes.\n- The seal change. Commit b687ec5f changes only the three literals and keeps every route and gate assertion. I recomputed each seal outside the builder's worktree with the test's own code. On main, judge.ts and genesis.ts give the old file seals, and the named seal for Scope in core.ts gives the old literal. At the head they give exactly the three new literals. The seal script itself does not change. The evidence records Hugh's direct approval of patch 40864da3…, and planner act 3655896d assigns the seal review to me.\n- What the sealed sources change. judge.ts changes only its imports, passes `definition` to `giving`, reads the grant mark through `nativeMark(definition, act.grant, \"grant\")` at the same position, and passes `definition` to `actionOf`. genesis.ts makes the same grant-mark change. core.ts passes the definition to one call. No check, check order, fault mapping or authority decision moves.\n- The gate. I read gate.exit at the gated source 6da48104, tree bd574062: \"exit 0\". result.json records Node 135, Counting 56, Plain 4,020 with one skip and Native 1,113 with two skips, with no report error and no unhandled error. before.json and after.json are byte-equal: clean status, 4,214 tracked inputs, lockfile 5a717d43 and gate.sh 001c4b10, which equal the files at 6da48104. receipt.json records unchanged source and no owned process left. Merge b98090cd brings in S1 main and keeps the gated tree. After it, only the note and two manifests change, so docs/testing.md needs no new gate.\n- The Page module. GitHub reports run 42442926609 (Page browser scripts, one dispatch) as successful on 6da48104, with every step successful. The note keeps the first collector's refusal separate from the complete records. The asset freshness test passed in the gate's plain phase, and assets.ts has not changed since. Addendum 474dc610 covers assets.ts.\n- The evidence. The three manifests that the note cites by hash match it. All nine manifests hold 388 files, which match their sizes and digests and are read-only, and the credential scan finds no match. Each control fails by assertion: the two Native and the two capability ownership cases on M6, and the duplicate-callback control, whose callback counts double.\n- My M6 notes. Execution now reads a Native send's `always` from the admitted node (sends.ts line 90). `formOf` and the `clauses` lookup are gone. The repeated `sendPlan` call in sendOrigin moves to M8, as the note says.\n- The tests. No case or deadline is removed. Three lines in the four derive test files change, and each becomes an equal or stricter check. The new cases compare whole judgments.\n- Semantics. An independent read of the derive, replay and scope source against main, with probes on extracted trees, found these equal on both trees:\n  - validation of 1,406 definitions: the corpus, the mark-form cases and ten capability shapes, compared by digest, marks, underived forms and problems;\n  - 24 Native scenarios across all seven places: judgments, callback order, receivers and arguments, missing and non-callable rules, the clock rule, outcome settles and copied-send clauses, and founding genesis;\n  - 16 capability variants: argument order, duplicates, empty and absent lists, shadowed binders, `{const: null}`, `{none: true}`, a non-list `each`, an unimplemented version checked before arguments, `from` and `fromItems`, hold@1, hold@2 and device-command@1;\n  - the observer at budgets −1, 0, 1, 1e308, ±Infinity, NaN, a string and 2.5, with throwing, nested and re-entrant judgments. Every callback runs exactly once, and no state remains after a judgment returns or throws. Only tests import the observer.\n\nF1 (does not block; M8 must fix). `nativeMark` (program/native.ts line 76) returns null for a definition object that no validation admitted. Main's `markOf` read the mark from the source shape. In judge.ts that fails closed: the act refuses `bad-intent`. In genesis.ts (line 196), the founding grant rule is skipped without a refusal, and only the later body lookup throws. fields.ts line 95 still uses `markOf` to skip the data check for a mark type, so a miss leaves such a field with neither check. No production source builds a ValidDefinition outside validation, and M5 and M6 already refuse bodies of an unadmitted definition, so no room reaches this. Make the lookup throw when the definition has no admission record, or when the source is a mark with no captured boundary.\n\nF2 (does not block; M8 must fix). runClause (handlers.ts lines 594 to 606) no longer throws \"result clause was not captured by its validation\" when a clause has effect forms but no captured structure. It now runs the clause with no effects. Every admitted lookup finds the structure, so no definition reaches this. Restore the assertion, so that a future lookup miss stops the result instead of dropping its effects.\n\nSome declaration values are still read live after admission: the source objects `act.grant` and `also`, field and slot types, `handler.bound` in `selectorOf`, the outcome kind, `origin` and `observes` rows in settle.ts lines 217 and 221 and in `rowsOfKind`, and `row.effects` in `windowOf`. The note's statement that outcome lookup uses captured declarations is therefore partial. Only a mutation after admission reaches these, and M8 owns the final orchestration.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Each of the seven Native places has one admitted record, and the body instructions point at it instead of copying it. Capability arguments are closed plans with their version. The observer only records, and it cannot choose a body or call a callback again. F1 and F2 come from the same pattern: a lookup that misses now returns null where it should refuse.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The protected judge and genesis keep every check in its order, and the seal values are the parser's real output for the reviewed sources. Rejected declarations never reach the admitted records. F1 skips a founding grant check only for a definition object that no validation produced, and a later check still stops that genesis.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Four notes:\n\n1. lists.ts keeps `covered` and its `rangePlan` import with no callers.\n2. Nothing sets or reads `Judging.elementTypes`, and `Judging.elements` serves only observes.ts line 192.\n3. `actionOf` keeps its `markOf` fallback only for test fixtures.\n4. The observer coerces a string budget and rounds 2.5 up to three events. Rejecting a non-integer budget would make the contract plain.\n\nThe non-callable rule now faults with the `Reflect.apply` message instead of \"rule.run is not a function\". The public judgment does not change. Parent 035 stays open through M8. This approval authorizes no deployment and closes no live acceptance.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8185a5a34e689383aca